---
title: Example · Store platform layers
config:
  look: handDrawn
  handDrawnSeed: 5
  theme: dark
  themeVariables:
    mainBkg: "#333333"
    clusterBkg: "#242424"
  themeCSS: |
    /* hand-drawn block arrows skip the node fill rule */
    .rough-node polygon { fill: #333333; stroke: #b3b3b3; }
---
%% `columns N` sets the grid (omitted means one row, `auto`); `id:N` spans N columns; `space` or `space:N` leaves cells empty, which also gives edges room.
%% `block:id:N … end` nests a sub-grid; choose block when grid position carries meaning, flowchart when only links do.
%% Shapes use flowchart brackets (`( )` `([ ])` `[[ ]]` `[( )]` `(( ))` `> ]` `{ }` `{{ }}` `[/ /]` `[\ \]` `[/ \]` `[\ /]` `((( )))`); `id<["label"]>(down)` is a block arrow, also `up` `left` `right` `x` `y` and pairs such as `(x, down)`.
%% Links: `-->` arrow · `---` plain · `-- "text" -->` labelled.
block
  columns 3
  web(["Web app"]) space mobile(["Mobile app"])
  space:3
  gateway{{"API gateway · spans 3 columns"}}:3
  space routes<["routes to services"]>(down) space
  block:services:3
    columns 3
    orders["Order service"] payments["Payment service"] stock["Inventory service"]
  end
  space:3
  ordersDb[("Order DB")] queue[["Event queue"]] cache[("Stock cache")]

  web --> gateway
  mobile --> gateway
  orders --> ordersDb
  payments -- "publishes" --> queue
  stock --- cache

  classDef em fill:#173d25,stroke:#86efac
  classDef db fill:#1c2f4a,stroke:#93c5fd
  classDef cache fill:#163a40,stroke:#67e8f9
  classDef queue fill:#2e2650,stroke:#c4b5fd
  class orders em
  class ordersDb db
  class cache cache
  class queue queue
